Steps:
[AUTH] POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token (grant_type=password, username={{ADMIN_EMAIL}}, password={{ADMIN_PASSWORD}}) to obtain an admin Bearer token BEFORE any MFA setting is touched. Export it as VC_ADMIN_TOKEN so init() of mfa-fixtures.mjs reuses it instead of a password grant
[SETUP] import scripts/seed-data/auth/mfa-fixtures.mjs: init(); runId = a fresh 3-16 char [a-z0-9] string (it lands in emails, store ids and names)
[SETUP] runIdC = a second fresh 3-16 char [a-z0-9] string
[SETUP] READ ONLY: GET {{BACK_URL}}/api/platform/settings/MultiFactorAuthentication.Enabled with the admin Bearer and require false (or unset); if it is on the case is BLOCKED (a global that is on decides store-less requests), never FAIL; the case writes no global setting
[SETUP] storeA = createMfaStore(runId, {mode: 'CustomerChoice'}) - an AGENT-TEST-MFA-<runId> store cloned from {{STORE_ID}} with an unresolvable .invalid URL (it can never capture the shared storefront); capture storeA.id and read StoreMode back ('CustomerChoice')
[SETUP] storeC = createMfaStore(runIdC, {mode: 'AdminManaged'}) - an AGENT-TEST-MFA-<runIdC> store cloned from {{STORE_ID}} with an unresolvable .invalid URL (it can never capture the shared storefront); capture storeC.id and read StoreMode back ('AdminManaged')
[SETUP] userAcc = createMfaAccount({runId: runId, store: storeA, kind: 'customer-confirmed'}) - an @example.com account with password {{DEFAULT_TEST_PASSWORD}} whose flags the creator verified; capture userAcc.email, userAcc.userId
[SETUP] orgAcc = createMfaAccount({runId: runIdC, store: storeC, kind: 'org-member-own-store'}) - an @example.com account with password {{DEFAULT_TEST_PASSWORD}} whose flags the creator verified; capture orgAcc.email, orgAcc.userId, orgAcc.orgs[0].id
[CAPTURE] unknownStoreId = AGENT-TEST-MFA-<runId>-nostore (a store that does not exist)
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/api/notifications/journal with the admin Bearer and JSON body {"notificationType":"MfaSignInEmailNotification","keyword":userAcc.email,"sort":"createdDate:desc","take":20}; capture the number of rows as userBefore and add the ids of those rows to seen(userAcc)
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/api/notifications/journal with the admin Bearer and JSON body {"notificationType":"MfaSignInEmailNotification","keyword":orgAcc.email,"sort":"createdDate:desc","take":20}; capture the number of rows as orgBefore and add the ids of those rows to seen(orgAcc)
--- LAYER: Both modes Off (the default): not asked ---
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token (application/x-www-form-urlencoded): grant_type=password, scope=offline_access, storeId=unknownStoreId, username=userAcc.email, password={{DEFAULT_TEST_PASSWORD}}
[CAPTURE] userOff = the response (status, error, errors[0].code, twoFactorToken, access_token presence)
[HTTP] POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token (application/x-www-form-urlencoded): grant_type=password, scope=offline_access, storeId=unknownStoreId, username=orgAcc.email, password={{DEFAULT_TEST_PASSWORD}}
[CAPTURE] orgOff = the response (status, error, errors[0].code, twoFactorToken, access_token presence)
